{
  "an10.108:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 10.108 ",
  "an10.108:0.2": "11. Perceptions for Ascetics ",
  "an10.108:0.3": "Doctors ",
  "an10.108:1.1": "“Mendicants, doctors prescribe a purgative for eliminating illnesses stemming from disorders of bile, phlegm, and wind. ",
  "an10.108:1.2": "There is such a purgative, I don’t deny it. ",
  "an10.108:1.3": "But this kind of purgative sometimes works and sometimes fails. ",
  "an10.108:2.1": "I will teach a noble purgative that works without fail. Relying on that purgative, sentient beings who are liable to rebirth, old age, and death, to sorrow, lamentation, pain, sadness, and distress are freed from all these things. ",
  "an10.108:2.2": "Listen and apply your mind well, I will speak.” ",
  "an10.108:2.3": "“Yes, sir,” they replied. ",
  "an10.108:2.4": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "an10.108:3.1": "“And what is the noble purgative that works without fail? ",
  "an10.108:4.1": "For one of right view, wrong view is purged. ",
  "an10.108:4.2": "And the many bad, unskillful qualities produced by wrong view are purged. ",
  "an10.108:4.3": "And because of right view, many skillful qualities are fully developed. ",
  "an10.108:5.1": "For one of right purpose, wrong purpose is purged. … ",
  "an10.108:5.2": "For one of right speech, wrong speech is purged. … ",
  "an10.108:5.3": "For one of right action, wrong action is purged. … ",
  "an10.108:5.4": "For one of right livelihood, wrong livelihood is purged. … ",
  "an10.108:5.5": "For one of right 